        "v": 5,
        "title": "DeepSeek Chat added as backend for Lite mode",
        "summary": "DeepSeek Chat (`deepseek-chat`) now powers Lite mode requests via new `backend/src/deepseek-api.ts` streaming handler. This replaces Claude Haiku for `costMode === 'lite'` in `main-prompt.ts` and `request-files-prompt.ts`, using OpenAI-compatible API with Helicone proxying. Cost tracking in `message-cost-tracker.ts` adds DeepSeek token rates ($0.14/$0.28 per M input/output), while `common/src/constants.ts` exports `deepseekModels`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:39:09.637Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the Lite mode (a cheaper, faster option), your requests are now handled by DeepSeek Chat instead of the previous model. When you type in Lite mode, responses will come from this new model, which costs less per message. The system now tracks the cost of these responses at the new rates, so billing reflects the cheaper pricing.",
